SPU lifter: a brsl whose link register is a continuation the callee calls back is a branch, not a call (--callback-brsl).

Nexus 1.01 newgame-level halts at ~350 s: ig lane 0, img -1, pc 0x04D10, host_depth 2000 (nexus-7105, nexus-wwatch2 and
nexus-level all identical; the lane idled at depth 0 one second before). The depth grows inside ONE run of job 0x00C21400,
not per job, so 7099's framed job call cannot help. Cause: the job's packer idiom. F at 0x6818 does
`brsl $r77, 0x5E40` (0x68A4; also 0x5ED8 0x5FD8 0x6184 0x64D0 0x65F0 0x6718 0x69B4); the packer calls the continuation
back per batch (`bisl $r78, $r77` at 0x5E54/0x5E78, the producer at 0x68A8 returns with `bi $r78` at 0x6934) and leaves
with `bi $r0` (0x5E8C) to F's CALLER (0x5728). On hardware the brsl only loads r77. Lifted as a host call bracket it waits
for 0x68A8, receives 0x5728, and the drain interprets on from there inside it ([pm-end] `N:05728/204 J:070AC/204`): two
host frames per packer call never close. The same job is in A4O 1.03 (0x00D3C580, packer 0x6190), FFA 1.05 and ACiT 1.20
(0x00B9B100, packer 0x6450): A4O's luminopolis leak (~386 per burst, closed at the job's exit by 7099) is this idiom too.
ToD and QfB igcollbroadspu carry it as well (8 sites each); they are only changed when lifted with the flag.

compute_callback_brsls: a `brsl/brasl $rN` (N != 0) is a callback brsl when every path from its target (fallthrough,
direct and conditional branches, calls stepped over) ends in a `bi $r0` return, rN is never written there and is the
target of a bisl. Anything else (a `bi $rN` link return, a computed branch, iret/stop, a target outside the image, more
than 4096 steps) keeps the bracket. --callback-brsl lifts those sites as `rN = link; branch` (goto or SPU_HOP); without
the flag the output is byte-identical (checked on Nexus 0x00C21400). tools/spu/lift_igjobs.py passes it for the kernel
and every job (table key "callback_brsl": false opts out). Static scan of all 126 lifted R&C SPU images: 8 sites each in
nexus101 igjob_00c21400, a4o igjob_00d3c580, ffa igjob_00dac680, acit120 igjob_00b9b100, tods/qfb igcollbroadspu; none
elsewhere.
Host test port/rc/tests/run_igjob_callback_brsl_test.sh: a synthetic kernel + job with the idiom lifted by lift_igjobs.py
and run on the real runtime (image -1 policy context): with 7106 n = 1/10/1500/6000 calls end at the stop with r3 = 5n,
depth 0, no halt, no 7099 unwind; the control (callback_brsl false) needs a 7099 unwind at n = 10 and halts with
[spu-depth] host_depth 2000 at n = 1500. Source: SPU notes, 2026-11-19.

